Run postgreSQL db with persistent data.

	1. Create a volume named pg-data
	2. Run PosgreSQL 16 with:
		Name: mydb
		Password: secretpass (via POSTGRES_PASSWORD env variable)
		The volume mounted to /var/lib/postgresql/data
		restart policy: unless-stopped
	3. Create a test db: docker exec mydb psql -U postgres -c "CREATE DATABASE testdb;"
	4. Verify: docker exec mydb psql -U postgres -c "/l"
	5. Remove the container 
	6. Create a new container with the same volume
	7. Verify the database still exists

	Verify: after recreating the container, testdb should still appear in the database list.

